      "description": "Watch GO Ahead Eagles vs Willem II highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The atmosphere at De Adelaarshorst was buzzing as two Eredivisie sides looked to establish their dominance early in the campaign. Fans gathered in anticipation of a tactical battle that promised plenty of action and strategic intrigue. Early Stakes and a Swift Response On August 8, 2026 , the match kicked off with high intensity as Willem II struck first to silence the home crowd. In the 13th minute, Devin Haen found the back of the net with a clinical right-footed finish, capitalize on an assist from Nathan Tjoe-A-On . The early goal forced Go Ahead Eagles to raise their tempo, and they began to dominate territory in search of an equalizer. That equalizer arrived exactly at the half-hour mark. Melle Meulensteen turned provider, setting up Soeren Tengstedt for a composed right-footed strike that leveled the scores. While the first half saw a few nervous moments and yellow cards for Dean James and Julius Dirksen , both teams headed into the break with the match finely balanced, though the momentum was clearly shifting toward the hosts. Second-Half Surge Decides the Day The second half belonged entirely to Go Ahead Eagles , who unleashed a devastating offensive spell. The comeback was completed in the 61st minute when Melle Meulensteen unleashed a powerful shot from outside the box to beat the keeper. Before Willem II could catch their breath, substitute Erik Flataker made an immediate impact, scoring with his right foot in the 63rd minute following a setup by Victor Edvardsen . The final blow came in the 69th minute as Julius Dirksen joined the scoresheet with a left-footed effort, assisted by the creative Mathis Suray . Controlling a massive 69% of the ball possession, the home side managed the remaining minutes with professional ease. Despite a late yellow card for Ismael Mouhoul , the result was never in doubt as the Eagles closed out a comprehensive performance."
